The private method and the internal dependencies make it difficult to test the exact line directly. Also, the refactor tool is not available to add test seams. The UpdateChannel enum is protected, so I cannot use it directly in the test.

I will write a test for the public RunAsync method that triggers the version check and indirectly causes the LogWarning calls. I will mock the dependencies to simulate the scenario where a newer stable version is available and verify the Logger.LogWarning calls.

I will submit this test now. It will cover the Logger.LogWarning call on line 325 indirectly by exercising the public API. I will also add the necessary using directives and minimal stubs for missing types. I will avoid referencing protected enum directly by using reflection or string matching in the test verification. 

